{"node_id": "real_071_batch_66_NIHMLPWinter2021_21_HY_001", "node_type": "evidence", "status": "HYBRID_SHADOW_CANDIDATE", "unit_type": "TEXT", "source_atom_ids": ["D0004"], "source_fragment_ids": ["D0004_F001"], "source_visual_bundle_ids": [], "plain_text": "Some of the greatest challenges in patient care\ninvolve helping people improve their quality of\nlife as they cope with a serious illness. Providing\ntheir families with support and, at the end of life,\ngrieving, can also be hard.", "semantic_text": "Some of the greatest challenges in patient care involve helping people improve their quality of life as they cope with a serious illness. Providing their families with support and, at the end of life, grieving, can also be hard.", "visual_description": null, "geometry_members": [{"member_id": "D0004_geometry", "bbox": [98, 520, 729, 714], "bbox_source": "dolphin_v2_resized_image_pixels", "source_atom_id": "D0004"}], "native_visual_components": [], "production_modified": false, "visual_description_status": "UNVERIFIED_RETRIEVAL_HINT", "node_policy": "bounded-v2", "scoring_mode": "embedding_geometry", "hybrid_model_decision_file": "/hkfs/home/project/hk-project-p0025545/dv3352/Project/remote_runs/node-first-realpdf-20261118/output/nodes_prepared_incremental_non_nasa_after_all_parse_20261119/batch_83/hybrid/real_071_batch_66_NIHMLPWinter2021/page_0021/decisions.json"}
{"node_id": "real_071_batch_66_NIHMLPWinter2021_21_HY_002", "node_type": "evidence", "status": "HYBRID_SHADOW_CANDIDATE", "unit_type": "TEXT", "source_atom_ids": ["D0005"], "source_fragment_ids": ["D0005_F001"], "source_visual_bundle_ids": [], "plain_text": "For that reason, studying ways to\ncomfort and care for these people\nis important, says Jeri Miller, Ph.D.,\nchief of the Office of End-of-Life\nand Palliative Care Research at\nthe National Institute of Nursing\nResearch (NINR).", "semantic_text": "For that reason, studying ways to comfort and care for these people is important, says Jeri Miller, Ph.D., chief of the Office of End-of-Life and Palliative Care Research at the National Institute of Nursing Research (NINR).", "visual_description": null, "geometry_members": [{"member_id": "D0005_geometry", "bbox": [100, 765, 409, 940], "bbox_source": "dolphin_v2_resized_image_pixels", "source_atom_id": "D0005"}], "native_visual_components": [], "production_modified": false, "visual_description_status": "UNVERIFIED_RETRIEVAL_HINT", "node_policy": "bounded-v2", "scoring_mode": "embedding_geometry", "hybrid_model_decision_file": "/hkfs/home/project/hk-project-p0025545/dv3352/Project/remote_runs/node-first-realpdf-20261118/output/nodes_prepared_incremental_non_nasa_after_all_parse_20261119/batch_83/hybrid/real_071_batch_66_NIHMLPWinter2021/page_0021/decisions.json"}
{"node_id": "real_071_batch_66_NIHMLPWinter2021_21_HY_003", "node_type": "evidence", "status": "HYBRID_SHADOW_CANDIDATE", "unit_type": "TEXT", "source_atom_ids": ["D0006"], "source_fragment_ids": ["D0006_F001"], "source_visual_bundle_ids": [], "plain_text": "“ We want to make sure we\nunderstand what all populations in\nall care settings need. We also want\nto learn how best to communicate\na patient's situation to family\nmembers and other health care\nproviders, ” she says.", "semantic_text": "“ We want to make sure we understand what all populations in all care settings need. We also want to learn how best to communicate a patient's situation to family members and other health care providers, ” she says.", "visual_description": null, "geometry_members": [{"member_id": "D0006_geometry", "bbox": [100, 942, 405, 1114], "bbox_source": "dolphin_v2_resized_image_pixels", "source_atom_id": "D0006"}], "native_visual_components": [], "production_modified": false, "visual_description_status": "UNVERIFIED_RETRIEVAL_HINT", "node_policy": "bounded-v2", "scoring_mode": "embedding_geometry", "hybrid_model_decision_file": "/hkfs/home/project/hk-project-p0025545/dv3352/Project/remote_runs/node-first-realpdf-20261118/output/nodes_prepared_incremental_non_nasa_after_all_parse_20261119/batch_83/hybrid/real_071_batch_66_NIHMLPWinter2021/page_0021/decisions.json"}
{"node_id": "real_071_batch_66_NIHMLPWinter2021_21_HY_004", "node_type": "evidence", "status": "HYBRID_SHADOW_CANDIDATE", "unit_type": "TEXT", "source_atom_ids": ["D0007"], "source_fragment_ids": ["D0007_F001"], "source_visual_bundle_ids": [], "plain_text": "That's why NINR is funding\nresearch about the health risks\nand needs of family caregivers\nof persons with a serious illness.\nFamily caregivers can be anyone\nfrom a spouse or partner, child,\nneighbor, or friend. “These\ncaregivers are at greater risk\nof depression and poor health\nbecause they may be less likely to\ntend to their own needs,” says Dr.\nMiller.", "semantic_text": "That's why NINR is funding research about the health risks and needs of family caregivers of persons with a serious illness. Family caregivers can be anyone from a spouse or partner, child, neighbor, or friend. “These caregivers are at greater risk of depression and poor health because they may be less likely to tend to their own needs,” says Dr. Miller.", "visual_description": null, "geometry_members": [{"member_id": "D0007_geometry", "bbox": [101, 1115, 396, 1413], "bbox_source": "dolphin_v2_resized_image_pixels", "source_atom_id": "D0007"}], "native_visual_components": [], "production_modified": false, "visual_description_status": "UNVERIFIED_RETRIEVAL_HINT", "node_policy": "bounded-v2", "scoring_mode": "embedding_geometry", "hybrid_model_decision_file": "/hkfs/home/project/hk-project-p0025545/dv3352/Project/remote_runs/node-first-realpdf-20261118/output/nodes_prepared_incremental_non_nasa_after_all_parse_20261119/batch_83/hybrid/real_071_batch_66_NIHMLPWinter2021/page_0021/decisions.json"}
